<title>GERMANY: German Q2 steel output falls to 9.0 mln tonnes.</title>
<headline>German Q2 steel output falls to 9.0 mln tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1996-09-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany produced 9.013 million tonnes of steel in the second quarter, down 3.5 percent on the same period a year earlier, the national steel federation said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Incoming orders were, however, over seven percent higher in the second quarter at 8.921 million tonnes.</p>
<p>The federation gave the following figures for rolled steel (in million tonnes):</p>
<p>		     Q2 1996	  Q1 1996	  Q2 1995</p>
<p> Output		9.013	    8.512	    9.326</p>
<p> Incoming orders   8.921	    9.255	    8.280</p>
<p>NOTE -- Order books stood at 7.121 million tonnes in June. No comparative figures were given.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
</text>
